1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,850
This ₹3 lakh iPhone folds in half.

2
00:00:02,850 --> 00:00:04,867
But glass cracks when you bend it.

3
00:00:04,867 --> 00:00:05,450
So how?

4
00:00:05,450 --> 00:00:06,929
Let's open it up.

5
00:00:06,929 --> 00:00:09,200
It's just 5.2 mm thin.

6
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:11,404
Trick one: the screen isn't one sheet.

7
00:00:11,404 --> 00:00:12,970
It's about ten thin layers.

8
00:00:12,970 --> 00:00:15,813
Like a stack of paper, they slide past each other

9
00:00:15,813 --> 00:00:17,669
when it bends, so nothing snaps.

10
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:20,523
Trick two: the hinge.

11
00:00:20,523 --> 00:00:23,043
Over a hundred parts, gears and springs,

12
00:00:23,043 --> 00:00:25,185
under a 3D-printed titanium cover.

13
00:00:25,185 --> 00:00:28,020
When it closes, the screen doesn't fold flat.

14
00:00:28,020 --> 00:00:29,973
It curls into a teardrop shape.

15
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:34,281
But bend the same spot again and again,

16
00:00:34,281 --> 00:00:36,126
and it never goes perfectly flat.

17
00:00:36,126 --> 00:00:38,100
That's the crease you can feel.

18
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:39,899
So it doesn't fold like paper.

19
00:00:39,899 --> 00:00:41,279
It rolls like a poster.

20
00:00:42,350 --> 00:00:44,078
Follow InvisiTech for more.

21
00:00:44,078 --> 00:00:46,370
Like, comment and subscribe.
